Read every step row against the 'natural' and 'shuffled' rows (src.make_baselines): natural is the ceiling, shuffled the composition-matched floor. A step whose pLDDT sits at or below shuffled has learned composition and not structure.
DEGENERATE marks k13 repeat coverage above 2.0% (5x the natural row): repetitive sequences fold CONFIDENTLY, so a high pLDDT there is the metric being gamed, not a better model. Also compare the len column before believing a pLDDT gain -- short chains score higher.
